[00:00.00] On a hill far away stood an old rugged cross,
[00:13.00] An emblem of suffering and shame.
[00:21.00] And I love that old cross for the dearest and best,
[00:30.00] For a world of lost sinners was slain.
[00:39.00] So I'll cherish the old rugged cross,
[00:48.00] Till my trophies at last I lay down.
[00:57.00] I will cling to the old rugged cross,
[01:06.00] And exchange it someday for a crown.
[01:18.00] To the old rugged cross,
[01:33.00] I will ever be true,
[01:37.00] It's shame and reproach gladly bear.
[01:46.00] Then he'll call me someday to my home far away,
[01:55.00] For his glory forever I'll share.
[02:03.00] So I'll cherish the old rugged cross,
[02:12.00] Till my trophies at last I lay down.
[02:21.00] I will cling to the old rugged cross,
[02:30.00] And exchange it someday for a crown.
